#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to update your code to use BackendV2 instead of BackendV1."
msgstr "Cómo actualizar tu código para usar BackendV2 en lugar de BackendV1."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate from BackendV1 to BackendV2"
msgstr "Migrar de BackendV1 a BackendV2"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate from `BackendV1` to `BackendV2` {#migrate-from-backendv1-to-backendv2}"
msgstr "Migrar de `BackendV1` a `BackendV2` {#migrate-from-backendv1-to-backendv2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Qiskit [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) class has been deprecated and will be removed from service. This migration guide describes the small adjustments you need to make if you use a provider that upgraded from [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) to [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2).\n"
msgstr ""
"La clase [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) de Qiskit ha sido marcada como obsoleta y será eliminada del servicio. Esta guía de migración describe los pequeños ajustes que necesitas hacer si usas un\n"
"proveedor que actualizó de [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) a [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2).\n"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
" If you exclusively use `qiskit_ibm_runtime` and `qiskit_aer`, no action is needed.  The `qiskit_ibm_runtime` package has always used `BackendV2`, and `qiskit_aer` has used `BackendV2` since version 0.13.\n"
" </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "High-level changes in `BackendV2` {#high-level-changes-in-backendv2}"
msgstr "Cambios generales en `BackendV2` {#high-level-changes-in-backendv2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Qiskit [`Backend`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.Backend) model was designed to provide the Qiskit SDK with an abstraction\n"
"layer that enabled reasoning about quantum computers within the scope of the SDK. The first iteration of the model was introduced with the\n"
"[`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) class. This class stored the backend information in a series\n"
"of data containers, namely the [`BackendConfiguration`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.models.BackendConfiguration) and\n"
"[`BackendProperties`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.models.BackendProperties) classes.\n"
msgstr ""
"El modelo [`Backend`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.Backend) de Qiskit fue diseñado para proporcionar al SDK de Qiskit una capa de abstracción\n"
"que permitiera razonar sobre computadoras cuánticas dentro del alcance del SDK. La primera iteración del modelo se introdujo con la clase\n"
"[`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1). Esta clase almacenaba la información del backend en una serie de contenedores de datos, concretamente las clases\n"
"[`BackendConfiguration`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.models.BackendConfiguration) y\n"
"[`BackendProperties`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.models.BackendProperties).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) class redefined\n"
"user access for most backend properties to make them work with native Qiskit data structures and have flatter\n"
"access patterns. The core of the [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) model is the\n"
"[`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) class, a representation of the QPU that contains the transpilation constraints that Qiskit can use to optimize circuits for execution.\n"
msgstr ""
"La clase [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) redefinió el acceso del usuario a la mayoría de las propiedades del backend para\n"
"que funcionen con las estructuras de datos nativas de Qiskit y tengan patrones de acceso más simples. El núcleo del modelo\n"
"[`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) es la clase [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target), una representación de la QPU que contiene las restricciones\n"
"de transpilación que Qiskit puede usar para optimizar los circuitos antes de su ejecución.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Qiskit SDK has been updated to work exclusively with [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) inputs,\n"
"and most providers have upgraded from [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) to [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2). It is expected that existing providers will deprecate the old access where possible to provide a graceful migration, but eventually users will need to adjust their code.\n"
msgstr ""
"El SDK de Qiskit se ha actualizado para trabajar exclusivamente con entradas [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2), y la mayoría\n"
"de los proveedores han migrado de [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) a [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2). Se espera que los\n"
"proveedores existentes marquen como obsoleto el acceso antiguo cuando sea posible para facilitar una migración gradual, pero en última instancia\n"
"los usuarios necesitarán ajustar su código.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The principle behind [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) is\n"
"that most of the information about a backend is contained in its\n"
"[`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) object, and the backend's attributes often query\n"
"its `BackendV2.target` attribute to return information. However, in many cases the attributes only provide\n"
"a subset of information that the target can contain. For example, `backend.coupling_map`\n"
"returns a [`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap) constructed from the\n"
"[`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) accessible in the\n"
"`BackendV2.target` attribute. However, the target might contain\n"
"instructions that operate on more than two qubits (which can't be represented in a\n"
"[`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap)) or it might have instructions that only operate on\n"
"a subset of qubits (or two qubit links, for a two qubit instruction), which won't be\n"
"detailed in the full coupling map returned by\n"
"`BackendV2.coupling_map`. So depending on your use case,\n"
"it might be necessary to look deeper than just the equivalent access with\n"
"[`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2).\n"
msgstr ""
"El principio detrás de [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) es que la mayor parte de la información sobre un backend está\n"
"contenida en su objeto [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target), y los atributos del backend con frecuencia consultan su atributo `BackendV2.target`\n"
"para devolver información. Sin embargo, en muchos casos los atributos solo proporcionan un subconjunto de la información que el target puede\n"
"contener. Por ejemplo, `backend.coupling_map` devuelve un objeto [`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap) construido a partir del\n"
"[`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) accesible en el atributo `BackendV2.target`. Sin embargo, el target podría contener instrucciones que operen\n"
"sobre más de dos qubits (lo que no se puede representar en un [`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap)) o podría tener instrucciones que\n"
"solo operen sobre un subconjunto de qubits, lo cual no quedará detallado en el mapa de acoplamiento completo que devuelve `BackendV2.coupling_map`.\n"
"Por eso, dependiendo de tu caso de uso, puede ser necesario profundizar más allá del acceso equivalente con\n"
"[`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specific changes in `BackendV2` {#specific-changes-in-backendv2}"
msgstr "Cambios específicos en `BackendV2` {#specific-changes-in-backendv2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Most attributes have a direct replacement, simplifying the migration efforts. The only point of mismatch between interfaces is in the [`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap).\n"
msgstr "La mayoría de los atributos tienen un reemplazo directo, lo que simplifica el proceso de migración. El único punto de discrepancia entre las interfaces está en el [`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Following is a table of example access patterns in [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) and the new form\n"
"with [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2).\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación se muestra una tabla con ejemplos de patrones de acceso en [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) y la nueva forma con\n"
"[`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"important\">\n"
"Scroll to the right to see important notes.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"important\">\n"
"Desplázate hacia la derecha para ver las notas importantes.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|[`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) | [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) | Notes |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().n_qubits` | `backend.num_qubits`| |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().coupling_map` | `backend.coupling_map` | The return from [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) is a [`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap) object. In [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) it is an edge list. Also, this is just a view of the information contained in `backend.target` which may only be a subset of the information contained in the [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) object. |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().backend_name` | `backend.name` | |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().backend_version` | `backend.backend_version` | The `BackendV2.version` attribute represents the version of the abstract [`Backend`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.Backend) interface that the object implements, while `BackendV2.backend_version` is metadata about the version of the backend itself. |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().basis_gates` | `backend.operation_names` | The [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) returns a list of operation names contained in the `backend.target` attribute. The [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) might contain more information than can be expressed by this list of names. For example, some operations only work on a subset of qubits, and some names implement the same gate with different parameters.|\n"
"|`backend.configuration().dt`|`backend.dt`| |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().dtm`|`backend.dtm` | |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().max_experiments` |`backend.max_circuits` | |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().online_date` | `backend.online_date`| |\n"
"|`InstructionDurations.from_backend(backend)`|`backend.instruction_durations`| |\n"
"|`backend.defaults().instruction_schedule_map`|`backend.instruction_schedule_map`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().t1(0)`|`backend.qubit_properties(0).t1`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().t2(0)`|`backend.qubit_properties(0).t2`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().frequency(0)`|`backend.qubit_properties(0).frequency`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().readout_error(0)`|`backend.target[\"measure\"][(0,)].error`| In [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2), the error rate for the [`Measure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#measure) operation on a given qubit is used to model the readout error. However, a [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) object can implement multiple measurement types and list them separately in a [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target).|\n"
"|`backend.properties().readout_length(0)`|`backend.target[\"measure\"][(0,)].duration`| In [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2), the duration for the [`Measure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#measure) operation on a given qubit is used to model the readout length. However, a [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) object can implement multiple measurement types and list them separately in a [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target).|\n"
msgstr ""
"|[`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) | [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) | Notas |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().n_qubits` | `backend.num_qubits`| |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().coupling_map` | `backend.coupling_map` | Lo que devuelve [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) es un objeto [`CouplingMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.CouplingMap). En [`BackendV1`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/1.4/qiskit.providers.BackendV1) es una lista de aristas. Además, esto es solo una vista de la información contenida en `backend.target`, que puede ser únicamente un subconjunto de la información contenida en el objeto [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target). |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().backend_name` | `backend.name` | |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().backend_version` | `backend.backend_version` | El atributo `BackendV2.version` representa la versión de la interfaz abstracta [`Backend`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.Backend) que implementa el objeto, mientras que `BackendV2.backend_version` es metadato sobre la versión del backend en sí. |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().basis_gates` | `backend.operation_names` | [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) devuelve una lista de nombres de operaciones contenidas en el atributo `backend.target`. El [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) puede contener más información de la que puede expresarse con esta lista de nombres. Por ejemplo, algunas operaciones solo funcionan en un subconjunto de qubits, y algunos nombres implementan la misma puerta con distintos parámetros.|\n"
"|`backend.configuration().dt`|`backend.dt`| |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().dtm`|`backend.dtm` | |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().max_experiments` |`backend.max_circuits` | |\n"
"|`backend.configuration().online_date` | `backend.online_date`| |\n"
"|`InstructionDurations.from_backend(backend)`|`backend.instruction_durations`| |\n"
"|`backend.defaults().instruction_schedule_map`|`backend.instruction_schedule_map`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().t1(0)`|`backend.qubit_properties(0).t1`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().t2(0)`|`backend.qubit_properties(0).t2`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().frequency(0)`|`backend.qubit_properties(0).frequency`| |\n"
"|`backend.properties().readout_error(0)`|`backend.target[\"measure\"][(0,)].error`| En [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2), la tasa de error de la operación [`Measure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#measure) en un qubit determinado se usa para modelar el error de lectura. Sin embargo, un objeto [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) puede implementar múltiples tipos de medición y listarlos por separado en un [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target).|\n"
"|`backend.properties().readout_length(0)`|`backend.target[\"measure\"][(0,)].duration`| En [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2), la duración de la operación [`Measure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#measure) en un qubit determinado se usa para modelar la longitud de lectura. Sin embargo, un objeto [`BackendV2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.providers.BackendV2) puede implementar múltiples tipos de medición y listarlos por separado en un [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target).|\n"
